{
  "description": "Whole-word matching for keys that are not simple words (WorldInfoBuffer.matchKeys, world-info.js:337-366). Two entries per case, same key and same message, one with matchWholeWords true and one false, so the boundary rule and the plain-substring path are both pinned and neither depends on the engine's global default. The rule that decides every row: the boundary is `(?:^|\\W)(key)(?:$|\\W)` and JS `\\w` is ASCII-only, so `C++` matches inside `abcC++def` (both neighbours are `\\W`), a multi-word key such as `New York` degrades to a plain substring search, and a CJK key matches between ideographs precisely because the ASCII class does not count them as word characters.",
